// Title: Assembly DLL Creation Via AspNetCompiler
// Sigma ID: 4c7f49ee-2638-43bb-b85b-ce676c30b260
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-08-14 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution
// Description: Detects the creation of new DLL assembly files by "aspnet_compiler.exe", which could be a sign
//   of "aspnet_compiler" abuse to proxy execution through a build provider.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate assembly compilation using a build provider
// References:
//   - Internal Research
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_aspnet_temp_files.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\aspnet_compiler.exe" and (FolderPath contains "\\Temporary ASP.NET Files\\" and FolderPath contains "\\assembly\\tmp\\" and FolderPath contains ".dll")
